# Code Quality

- TypeScript strict mode; never use `any` to bypass types.
- Run `npm run validate` before opening PRs (format, lint, typecheck, test).
- Keep diffs focused; avoid unrelated refactors.
- Match existing naming, imports, and file placement conventions.
- Server-only env parsing belongs in `src/lib/env.ts` and server modules.
- Use Zod for runtime validation at system boundaries (env, webhooks).
